• A complex number is a number in the form a + bi,
where a and b are real numbers, and i = [IMG:image14.wmf].
• For a complex number a + bi,
the real number a is called the real part and
the real number b is called the imaginary part.
• For any positive integer n,
if the remainder of n ÷ 4 is 1, then i ^{n} = i ^{1} = i;
if the remainder of n ÷ 4 is 2, then i ^{n} = i ^{2} = –1;
if the remainder of n ÷ 4 is 3, then i ^{n} = i ^{3} = –i;
if the remainder of n ÷ 4 is 0, then i ^{n} = i ^{4} = 1.
